WEBVTT

00:07:28.694 --> 00:07:30.863
to find out where
their feeding grounds are,

00:07:30.905 --> 00:07:33.657
and by doing this,
we are finding and discovering

00:07:33.699 --> 00:07:37.161
new seagrass meadows
in the Indian Ocean and the Red Sea,

00:07:37.161 --> 00:07:38.913
which were poorly studied.

00:07:39.246 --> 00:07:40.581
And in the Bahamas,

00:07:40.623 --> 00:07:42.917
we are now partnering with tiger sharks,

00:07:42.958 --> 00:07:44.752
because we found that in the Bahamas,

00:07:44.752 --> 00:07:47.963
tiger sharks spend
about 70 percent of their time

00:07:47.963 --> 00:07:49.924
cruising over seagrass meadows.

00:07:49.965 --> 00:07:52.927
And we instrumented,
last year, for the first time,

00:07:52.927 --> 00:07:56.514
a tiger shark with 360-degree cameras,

00:07:56.514 --> 00:08:00.184
which are sitting on the fin of the shark